claude says:
    func 208 "realloc() - it resizes an already-allocated memory block".
    func 260 "it removes a free memory block from the allocator's data structures".
    func 266 "UTF-8 decoder with Unicode character classification function".
    func 302 is malloc.
    func 311 "insert_free_chunk() - it adds a freed block back to the allocator and merges it with adjacent free blocks".
    func 348 "dynamic array/vector resize function - it grows the capacity of a data structure (likely a vector or dynamic array) when it runs out of space".
    func 405 is free.
    func 423 is memcpy.



